course: dictionary
lesson: 10505
title: Twice: two times, or double
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word twice has two main jobs. First, it counts times: «I rang twice» means I rang two times, so the phone rang, then I rang again. Second, it means double the amount, as in «twice as many» or «twice as much».
explain: When you see «twice as many as», multiply by 2. «Lily invited girls from both streets, and her mum had to buy twice as many party bags.» If there were 5 girls, her mum would buy 10 bags, because 5 × 2 = 10.
explain: Twice is also used in set phrases. «Twice a day» means two times each day, and «think twice» means stop and consider something carefully before you act. Read the words around twice to find which meaning fits.
fact: Twice means two times.
fact: Twice as many or twice as much means double the amount.
fact: «Twice as many as N» means N × 2.
fact: «Twice a day» means two times in one day.
fact: «Think twice» means consider carefully before you decide.
exercise: «I rang twice.» How many times did I ring? | Once | Ten times | *Two times | Three times
exercise: Sam has 4 marbles. Ben has twice as many. How many marbles does Ben have? | 16 | *8 | 6 | 2
exercise: Which phrase means to stop and consider carefully before you act? | *Think twice | Twice a day | Twice as many | Twice as much
test: «The wind grows quickly: wind twice as fast pushes about four times as hard.» If wind is 10 units fast, what speed is twice as fast? | 12 | *20 | 100 | 5
test: «Programmers write the same thing twice, and then a loop does the work.» What does twice mean here? | *Two times | Half as much | Once more and then stop forever | Very quickly
exam: «With 4 children each shaking hands once with every other child, there are 6 handshakes, because 4 × 3 = 12 counts each handshake twice.» What does twice mean in that sentence? | Once | Three times | *Two times | Half as many
